    <summary>Beautiful command-line tool for Letterboxd - pure Rust, no Python required</summary>
    <description>
lbxd v3.0.0 is a powerful command-line tool written in pure Rust that brings Letterboxd to your terminal.

## What's New in v3.0.0
- Pure Rust implementation - NO Python dependencies!
- Faster performance with native rustboxd library
- Simplified installation

## Features
- Interactive TUI for browsing complete movie collections
- View recent activity, ratings, and reviews for any user
- Search functionality for titles in user activity
- Movie database integration with TMDB
- Export data to JSON or Markdown formats
- Beautiful terminal display with poster images
- Configurable settings and user preferences
- Intelligent caching for offline access
- Cross-platform support (Windows, macOS, Linux)

## Quick Start
After installation, try:
- `lbxd recent username` - View recent activity
- `lbxd movie "Inception"` - Search for movies
- `lbxd browse username` - Interactive TUI mode
- `lbxd --help` - See all commands

## Requirements
- viu (optional, for terminal image display): `cargo install viu`

## API Keys
For movie search and poster display, get free API keys:
- TMDB: https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api
- OMDB: https://www.omdbapi.com/apikey.aspx
